System Monitor is BuzzOS's graphical process and resource manager.

The Processes view refreshes once per second and shows PID, process name,
scheduler state, sampled CPU usage, and resident user-memory mappings. Click a
column heading to sort, use the mouse wheel or arrow keys to navigate, and use
End Process to terminate the selected process. PID 0 and System Monitor itself
cannot be terminated from the application.

The Resources view shows 60-sample CPU and memory histories plus system uptime.
Pause freezes automatic updates; Refresh always takes a new sample.

BuzzOS currently has one immediate process-kill primitive rather than Linux
signals, priorities, users, cgroups, or per-process I/O counters. End Process
therefore performs an immediate process-wide termination.
